<title>UK: Jardine Int'l Motors H1 profits slip.</title>
<headline>Jardine Int'l Motors H1 profits slip.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30</p>
<p>			   (million US$ unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (cents)		7.18		   vs 16.57</p>
<p> Dividend (cents)	 1.20		   vs 1.20</p>
<p> Net income post tax    34.0		   vs 79.0</p>
<p>Note - The company said net income in the year earlier period included an exceptional profit of $44 million. Excluding the exceptional item, the profit fall was 3 percent.</p>
<p>Jardine International Motors Holdings Limited chairman Simon Keswick said the company's trading result for the full year &quot;is unlikely to match that of 1995.&quot;  </p>
<p> Pretax profit	    40.7		   vs 85.7</p>
<p> Turnover		   985.1		  vs 956.3</p>
<p> Operating result	 42.1		   vs 46.6</p>
<p> Exceptional		nil		    vs 43.8</p>
<p> Interest		   2.2		    vs 3.8</p>
<p> Tax			  6.5		    vs 6.7</p>
<p> Retained profit	  28.6		   vs 73.4</p>
<p> Pay date		   October 30</p>
<p> Div registration date  October 4</p>
<p>Note - Keswick said the company continued to perform well but said the year result would come &quot;against a background of sustained difficult market conditions in Hong Kong and China.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 5427717</p>
</text>
